<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Feb industrial output down 5.5 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore Feb industrial output down 5.5 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output fell by 5.5 percent in February compared to the same month the year before, after falling a revised 6.9 per cent in January, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Feb 97	 Jan 97	  Dec 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	-5.5	   -6.9	   -0.6</p>
<p>    Electronics		  -7.8	  -11.1	   -2.6</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	-11.9	   -2.8	    9.7</p>
<p>    Paints, pharmaceuticals  26.5	    0.3	   -3.8</p>
<p>    Industrial chems/gas	4.3	    3.5	    6.5</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics -12.4	   -3.6	    8.7</p>
<p>    Transport equipment     -11.2	   -3.6	    8.0</p>
<p>    Fabricated metals	  -8.3	   -6.8	   -6.0</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	-2.3	    0.6	   -3.5</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	-6.8	   -4.3	    1.3</p>
<p>    Plastic products	  -12.2	  -22.4	  -24.3</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
